Day 3 of the hashtag#60DayClaudeChallenge 🚀
Today’s lesson: Role-Based Prompting completely changed the quality of AI responses.
Instead of asking Claude a question normally, I tested the same prompt through different perspectives:
🔹 No Role
🔹 Founder Persona
🔹 Developer Persona
Question:
“How can I launch a successful mobile app?”
Here’s what happened:
✅ Without a role:
The response stayed broad and generic—useful, but designed for a general audience.
✅ As a Founder:
The answer shifted toward market validation, customer acquisition, growth strategy, retention, and building a sustainable business.
✅ As a Developer:
The response became more technical—covering architecture, tech stack choices, testing, deployment, and scalability.
My biggest takeaway:
AI doesn’t just answer questions—it adapts to perspective.
The way you frame the role shapes the depth, priorities, and direction of the output. One question can unlock completely different insights depending on who the AI is asked to become.
Role-Based Prompting turns AI into the specialist you need at that moment—Founder, Developer, Product Manager, HR Manager, Marketer, Consultant, and more.
Today’s learning:
Better prompts don’t just improve answers—they improve thinking.
